From: Ben Richard <143630488+benrichard-amd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIOpen: backport hipconv constexpr evaluation fix

Upstream: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries/commit/37920953b271d40f1cce9f2ab38d5e4d68c0cd2b
Upstream-PR: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries/pull/11989 (merged)
Upstream-Commit: 37920953b271d40f1cce9f2ab38d5e4d68c0cd2b

Backport the complete merged change, stripping only projects/miopen.
The PR description proposed raising -fconstexpr-steps, but the merged
commit removes the expensive rounds_are_rungs assertion. Keep the actual
upstream change; the other layout assertions and runtime algorithm remain.
No prerequisite source changes are needed on therock-10.1.

diff --git a/src/hipconv/src/arch/cdna4/direct/direct_wgrad/lds_layout.h b/src/hipconv/src/arch/cdna4/direct/direct_wgrad/lds_layout.h
--- a/src/hipconv/src/arch/cdna4/direct/direct_wgrad/lds_layout.h
+++ b/src/hipconv/src/arch/cdna4/direct/direct_wgrad/lds_layout.h
@@ -284,9 +284,6 @@ struct TransposeSwizzle
     static_assert(addressings_agree(),
                   "TransposeSwizzle::offset_uint2_shifted does not reach the slot "
                   "offset_uint2 names for the same element");
-    static_assert(rounds_are_rungs(),
-                  "a round of the transpose read is not a filter shift of the round before "
-                  "it, so the read is not a ladder and displacement() does not describe it");
 
     static constexpr bool is_bank_conflict_free(int num_shifts)
     {
